WEBVTT

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:16.410
<i>After a fight, we go out for a good dinner.</i>

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.580
<i>We've been doing so since before we got married.</i>

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.290
This is horrible.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.450
People said the food was good, so my hopes were high,

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.720
but not a single dish was anything special.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.130
Teo, people can hear you.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:36.410
You think? I thought it was quite good.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.620
You'd better rethink your definition of good.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.950
Otherwise I won't let you prep the ingredients.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.990
It does look like the chef has changed here.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.180
I was hoping you could learn a thing or two, Nicoletta.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.810
Oh well. 'Twas a waste of time.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.980
It wasn't as bad as they said.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.480
Sure, the quality dropped a little bit, but...

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.940
That wasn't your first time there?

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:18.620
Oh, that's right. I'm sure one of your midnight liaisons began there.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.760
Weren't we going there to celebrate making up?

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:22.570
Yes.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:26.470
But you're not out of the doghouse yet.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.470
Gelato!

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:32.700
You want me to freeze?

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:15.140
A Husband and Wife

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.900
<i>If you ever find yourself in Rome, go look for it...</i>

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:24.120
<i>The mysterious ristorante full of bespectacled gentlemen.</i>

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.950
This wine is pretty good.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.660
Maybe I'll take another glass.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.940
Sure, as soon as you finish that one.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.390
Thanks.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:42.890
I wish my husband would do these things for me.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:46.130
An expensive wine is nice from time to time.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.450
Can you recommend me something?

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.410
If you're looking for a recommendation...

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.580
Gigi.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.540
What do you like?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:57.170
He's a veteran sommelier.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.030
Wow.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:00.040
And your budget.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.660
Umm...

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.940
I wouldn't give her a Tuscan red.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:08.630
Perhaps a Piemonte? The recent whites have been selling well.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.720
Oh, the Sardinians go well with seafood, too.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.560
The whites from Le Marche go well with seafood pasta dishes.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.560
Hey, Lucia.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.280
Oh, Gianna, you're here too.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.290
You know, yesterday I saw your husband with some woman.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:23.300
Again? Once a playboy, always a playboy, huh?

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.820
He's always talking up the women at the store.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.330
I'm OK with it as long he doesn't get serious.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:34.240
Yeah, but it wasn't the first time I've seen him with a woman.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:34.840
What?

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.230
And this was the same woman.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.750
Man, it's freezing out there.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.820
Oh, something smells great.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.300
I rented us a DVD.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.810
I saw a good movie the other day.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.270
Oh yeah? What was it about?

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:02.120
About a husband who sneaks off to cheat on his wife and what she does afterwards.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:07.060
Oh, I'm not talking about you.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.920
I mean, you're just extra nice to girls.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.170
It's not like you're cheating on me or anything.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:15.290
So, there was this scene in the film.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.870
The husband decides to come home for once.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:22.500
The wife is hard at work at dinner. Suddenly she breaks a bottle of wine.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:28.250
The shards of glass end up in the pasta, and the husband eats them.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:30.220
She didn't do it on purpose, of course.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.890
Then, the husband storms off, in a fit of rage.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:37.510
That scene really left a deep impression in my mind.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.340
You don't say?

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:45.940
Oh dear. I broke the wine bottle.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:51.960
Don't worry. The shards didn't get in the pasta.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:54.650
We have another bottle, anyway.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:55.950
Oh, right.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:02.000
<i>I knew it. He has a mistress.</i>

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:06.190
How long have you been married?

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:09.330
Two years. And we dated for two years before that.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.030
He's been obsessed with women since back then.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:15.140
And I don't mean that he was a serial dater.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:20.160
He works as a salesman and picks up lots of women who come to his store.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.140
But back then, he was just fooling around, right?

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:27.700
Yes. But this last discretion was the final straw.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:32.150
My friend told me to see a specialist and sent me to you.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:35.700
First, you'd divvy up your assets.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.320
Then, a three-year legal separation.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:42.030
After that, you can finally request a divorce.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.280
What?

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.770
Getting divorced takes a lot of time and energy,

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:49.570
so please make sure you're properly prepared.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:55.670
Oh, Furio's giving cooking lessons?

00:06:55.670 --> 00:07:00.150
Yes. He said he runs them on his days off at the restaurant.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.900
Well, do your best.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.220
Say you will and I'll give you extra.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.690
It's just some unsold things.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:06.310
I will!

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.000
You can count on me!

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.780
I'll get really good at cooking and Teo will see me in a new light!

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:16.330
OK, today's lesson will be beef stew with polenta.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:18.290
Are you ready?

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.200
Yes!

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:28.000
Well? Enjoying your first day?

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.330
You bet! It's a lot of fun and I'm learning a lot.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.130
That's great.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.210
Teach me lots, OK?

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.850
You got it.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:38.220
Just who do you think you are?!

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:39.980
Furio belongs to all of us!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:43.640
Wh-What? U-Uh... I'm sorry.

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:52.420
That was tough in there.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:55.390
Most of the women are big fans of Furio.

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:58.590
Looks like it. And you're not, huh?

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.170
Yeah. I wouldn't really call myself a fan.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:05.660
You're the new apprentice at the ristorante, right?

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.910
I heard about you from Vito.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.560
Uh, umm...

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:12.050
I'm Marina, Vito's wife.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:13.550
What?!

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:17.130
He's so used to haute cuisine,

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:20.130
so I'm coming here to get better at cooking.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.270
Nice to meet you.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:22.880
O-Oh, I see.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.440
Nice to meet you.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:30.210
Man, was that a shocker!

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:34.150
She's no older than I am - Vito's wife.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:38.670
But still, she's not uncomfortable?

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:39.610
Huh?

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.720
You know...

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:45.690
See?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.460
Good point.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.240
It wouldn't sit right with me.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.680
I mean, Vito's really popular with the ladies,

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.210
and he's so much older than her.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:01.830
Well, the only ones who know what goes on between a married couple is the husband and wife.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:07.580
If it bothers you, why don't you ask Vito himself?

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:15.630
Wow, I'm honored.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:18.250
To think you'd worry about us so much.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.030
I'll leave it to your imagination.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:25.850
For I worship all the women of the world.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:27.360
I beg your pardon?!

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.420
Relax, relax.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:32.150
Well, I can't help it if you're concerned.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:36.550
But you know, I was the one who asked <i>her</i> out.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:37.710
Seriously?

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.900
Yes.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:42.790
It was a chance encounter of destiny, in the gym I used to go to.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.810
'Twas love at first sight.

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:48.190
I was after her.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:52.820
Then one day, there was a chance encounter at a karate dojo.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:57.570
And then, thanks to a puzzle magazine I had in a broken elevator,

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:00.840
I was able to pop the question.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:01.820
There you have it.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:05.320
How much of that am I supposed to believe?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:08.200
That's up to you, Nicoletta, dear.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.260
God!

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.280
Another glass, please.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:18.530
How about you tell her how you and Marina really got to know each other?

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:23.120
No, I cannot betray my wife's privacy.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.930
A gentleman must harbor a secret or two, don't you agree?

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:32.930
Now that you mention it, the day you requested is coming soon, isn't it?

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.970
Indeed. I'm counting on you.

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:44.180
So I need to prepare myself for the divorce, huh?

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:56.760
<i>He's all over the place, but it's not like I can't love him.</i>

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:59.750
<i>I mean, I do love him.</i>

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:05.260
<i>He just pisses me off. He really uses me.</i>

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.800
I should fool around, too.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:15.760
Buonasera.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.720
Buonasera.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.690
We've got customers at table two.

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:23.800
Antipasto, please.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:24.700
On it.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:28.200
Put a little extra salt in the second course.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:32.180
If I recall, her sister prefers a little stronger flavor.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:33.710
Huh? Sister?

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:35.230
Yes.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.730
You mean, Vito's sister?

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:41.830
Marina's sister.

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:45.060
She's visiting Marina while coming to see her folks.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:46.220
Her husband is here, too.

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:48.220
Yeah?

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:53.240
Tonight, we've got a dish made with a yogurt marinade and tomato sauce...

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:59.090
Say, that's Marina's sister and her husband?

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:00.910
The husband, he's...

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:03.610
Yes, he's from another country.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:07.060
They spend most of their time there.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.120
Oh, I see.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:14.050
The three of them used to live here, in town.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:14.920
Eh?

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:21.950
But well, there's a long story, but eventually she stayed behind, alone, here in Rome.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:26.970
When I first met her, Marina was still rough around the edges.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:33.200
But, ever since her and Vito got married, she's had a smile on her face, like that.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.840
Well, see you tomorrow. Ciao.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:42.870
Ciao.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:50.620
Should they be leaving Marina and them here?

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:53.820
Don't worry. The wife will catch up later.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.800
Oh, thank you for before.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.600
What?!

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:07.900
Huh?

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:16.590
Oh, there he is.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:18.720
I couldn't get into my place.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:21.760
I forgot the key and Lucia's not in.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.960
So you got lonely and came here?

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.610
Did Lucia stop by?

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:29.750
She sure did, and she left with Gigi just a few minutes ago.

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:34.040
Kinda like somebody we know who leaves his wife to go fool around.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.650
Who's Gigi?

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:40.540
Gigi, yeah... He's been a good man since the age of twenty-five.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:43.020
He's really tall.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:46.560
He might even be taller than me.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:50.150
Plus he's a master sommelier and a gifted conversationalist.

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.340
There's not a woman who'd turn him down.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.610
This is to pay you back for the advice you gave me. OK?

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.130
Are you always this quiet?

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:08.940
She got sick and tired of you cheating on her.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:12.510
So why not go home with that blonde beauty?

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:15.810
Or whatever works for him, huh?

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.630
You think you're so smart.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:18.690
Whatever.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:24.120
If I had to wager a guess, it's because she was frustrated, and just...

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.440
I'll give you a glass on the house for being dumped.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:33.130
Your wife is incredibly beautiful. Treat her well.

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:33.840
Huh?

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:37.220
You'd better listen to what your senior tells you.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:41.560
The two of you have a lot in common when it comes to women.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:45.130
Women just can't resist wanting to accompany me.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.630
Right, right!

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:49.240
They just decide they want to join me for dinner and such.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:53.740
Agreed. Which is why I never considered getting married.

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:57.480
I never wanted to hurt any one of them.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:02.070
The girls knew what kind of guy I am,

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:05.020
so only the ones looking for a good time approached me.

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:09.510
When those women weren't around, I was completely alone.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:13.520
But now, I've met my wife, whom I love.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:17.430
Sometimes, I get to thinking...

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:22.590
What would the two of us be doing, had we never met?

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:28.540
I'm almost positive I'd be spending my days all alone.

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:32.910
If what I'm describing would make you feel lonely,

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:37.280
you'd better stop doing what you're doing.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.140
And if you want to know about divorce, here's your guy.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:43.890
No better person to tell you about it than a divorcee.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:47.340
Oh, err... Umm... Nice to meet you.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:52.140
You don't want to hear Lucia say she's leaving you, do you?

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:02.650
There's something you need to keep in mind if you want a long, healthy marriage.

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:06.280
Think hard about it.

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:17.080
<i>She didn't come home again.</i>

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.140
I can't survive alone.

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:37.300
But, I don't want to sit here all day waiting

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.570
for my wife to come home from a date either!

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:41.390
This is Friday night!

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:52.960
Leaving again, are we?

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:57.580
"Again"? You've been out partying yourself!

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:00.990
I'm allowed to go shopping with friends, aren't I?

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:03.010
It just ran a little late.

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:05.380
Sure you weren't out with some guy?

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:06.750
A guy named Gigi.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:07.850
Gigi?

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:10.840
We had dinner the other night.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:11.670
So you admit it!

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:14.780
He's an older man and cute when he ate.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:18.170
He's older than my father, you know.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.040
What?

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:23.650
How about you? Which hot little thing are you going out with today?

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:26.800
I was waiting for you to come home!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.680
Dressed to go out?

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:33.710
Were you thinking about making things right with me?

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:50.040
Umm, I was thinking about what I need to do in order to have a long, healthy marriage.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:57.170
I've been pondering the same thing, these last few days.

00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:59.840
Did you figure it out?

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.500
I did.

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:10.350
But you need to stop having flings with random women.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.050
That's the first step.

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:16.870
What did you come up with?

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:20.440
Th-The same thing.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:22.880
I thought the same thing.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:28.520
I made a reservation for dinner tonight, thinking we'd make up.

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:31.880
I was waiting for you to come home.

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:35.420
Please forgive me, Lucia.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.380
I'll go get changed.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:44.060
What?

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:48.520
Umm, the landlord called me. I wonder what it's about.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:49.880
I'll be right back.

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:50.740
Get changed!

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:58.360
The one across the street... I've never set foot in there,

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:02.360
but I think I heard it's good.

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:05.010
A table!

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:06.990
Buonasera.

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:12.190
I can ready a table for you.

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.710
A couple just settled their tab.

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:22.330
Our top-notch sommelier, Gigi, will bring you an exquisite wine.

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:29.080
I believe he's already acquainted with your wife's tastes, so he can get started.

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:34.350
You <i>are</i> coming with your wife tonight, are you not?

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:40.460
This is a make-up dinner.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:45.170
Please give us the best food and wine you can, for her sake.

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:48.170
Absolutely.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:56.080
He was totally silent!

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:58.010
He never says a word!

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.850
That sommelier over there?

00:20:00.850 --> 00:20:01.350
Yes!

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:03.520
But he sure picks a good wine.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:08.310
Table five seems incredibly satisfied with dinner.

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:09.720
I think it's time for the dolce.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:10.480
On it.

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:21.040
What's that? You two are oddly getting along all of a sudden.

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:22.440
Yeah.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:25.930
No one charms the ladies like Vito.

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:29.300
Did he say some sweet things and sweep you off your feet?

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:31.080
Wouldn't you like to know?

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:33.890
<i>I think I figured it out.</i>

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:37.810
<i>There's only one person he truly loves.</i>

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:46.300
Vito.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:49.990
Oh, you'll have to excuse me.

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:57.790
I'm afraid my lovely wife and I have plans for the rest of the day.

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:15.950
A Special Day

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:13.300
It's almost like we're on a date, huh?

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:57.990
It's almost like you should... watch next time, huh?
